{
 "about": "Node60 power shapes, stage 1 (2026-11-04): inner planes (D12-1/D17 A), the 60 A entry path on B, In2, In3 and the F band (D18 A), VBAT_PROT at the disconnect FETs' sources, GND pours, and via fields at 0.65 A per 0.45/0.25 mm via (D12-6). Stage 2: each switch's VBB pad gets in-pad vias (filled and capped, DEC-027); each output a pour on B and F from its pins to its header's pin 1, OUTb the mirror image of OUTa, with mirrored via fields so both outputs of a switch get the same copper. D19 A (2026-11-04): the cells' small parts moved clear of the OUT exits; the B output pours reach north to y 104.5 beside the pins (F stays south of the VBAT_IN bar area). D20 A (2026-11-04): both battery terminals VBAT_IN, the entry mirrored about x 155. D21 C (2026-11-04): rows swapped so the ideal-diode FETs sit beside U201 (short DGATE): VBAT_IN an L from each ring to its north-row FET on B and In2 (In3 stays VBAT_PROT under it, toward U601/U801), VBAT_D the north band around the U201/U202 column, VBAT_Q2D the south band, VBAT_PROT from the south-row sources; vias in all four FET tabs. In3 VBAT_PROT (2026-11-04): the user cut it from the whole board to the power band; in3_sweep.py found the knee at x 72-238, y 71-122 (south of the switches carries current; the north and the far ends little). Small rails (D22 A and D23, 2026-11-04): 3V3_MAIN on In3 north of y 70.8, a 1V5_CORE island on In3 from U401's core to R303, VBAT_PROT fingers on In3 to L201 and U301, VBAT_FILT on B from L201 to U302; one via per small-rail pad (in the pad where it fits), U401's power and ground balls dogboned. Under U401 every via is 0.35/0.20 mm (via_overrides) so In3 keeps 0.15 mm webs; the caps under it sit on via pairs posed by power/bga_decaps.py (blocks/u401_decaps.poses.json), its power and ground balls dogboned at the cells that script chose (prefer, strict); H7 joins H6 on B, and C403, C404 and C419 reach their vias by short F tracks.",
